Subject: [PATCH 24/30] tcx: preserve overlapping blit source pixels

Both TCX blit spaces can copy overlapping regions of their own backing
store. memcpy gives undefined results, visible as damaged horizontal window
redraws with NEXTSTEP. Use memmove for 8-bit pixels, 24-bit pixels and raw
control planes. Preserve the distinction between BLIT and RBLIT.

Exercise both directions, self copies, every length 1..32, offsets -31..31,
both blit spaces and 8/24-bit display depths. The original model fails this
regression. The corrected model also preserves native Terminal contents
through a horizontal window-drag round trip.

Related independently proposed upstream change for ordinary BLIT:
https://www.mail-archive.com/qemu-devel@nongnu.org/msg1226322.html
This patch additionally covers RBLIT and includes regressions.

